        "timestamp": 1778174514,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Ici c'est Paris': Defending champions PSG 'on the verge of making history' Sport Issued on: 07/05/2026 - 19:21 Modified: 07/05/2026 - 19:32 With PSG on the brink of history, following a very tight semi-final match against German powerhouse Bayern-Munich, Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Victor Bolorunduro, Reporter for The Peninsula Qatar. The reigning European champions will now face Arsenal. According to Bolorunduro, PSG has discovered a \"cohesiveness\" and developed “a remarkable improvement from one match to another.” He places PSG’s current form within a broader narrative of European football evolution, once criticized for inconsistency, now “on the verge of retaining the title” for another year. ⚽ Champions League: Paris fans celebrate reaching the final 07/05/2026 Sport PSG visits Bayern for right to face Arsenal in Champions League final 06/05/2026 Sport 3 patients are being evacuated to Europe from ship with hantavirus outbreak 06/05/2026 Europe War in Ukraine: Russia attacks east and south Ukraine with over 100 drones 06/05/2026 Europe Injured Mbappe faces backlash over Sardinia trip before Clasico 06/05/2026 Sport Hantavirus-hit cruise ship heads to Spain to dock in Canary Islands 06/05/2026 Europe Kyiv says Russia broke unilateral ceasefire with drone and missile attacks 06/05/2026 Europe Russia launches deadly attack in Ukraine: At least 28 killed 06/05/2026 Europe Venice Biennale faces outcry over Israel and Russia's participation 06/05/2026 Europe"
